# DVC pointer files, Phase 6.4 (docs/revamp/BLOCKERS.md, heading 6.4). The corpus payload under
# data/corpus-20k and data/sources moved into DVC; a `.dvc` file is the only record of which
# content hash the remote holds for a path, so every one of them belongs in git even where the
# bytes beside it are ignored above. Several of those exclusions are `dir/*` globs, which would
# otherwise swallow the pointer file written next to the data and make `dvc add` refuse with
# "bad DVC file name ... is git-ignored". These two lines are last so they win over every rule
# above; a directory excluded outright (`dir/`) is never descended into and holds no pointer file.
!*.dvc
!.gitignore

# Two of the excluded directories above are excluded outright, so git does not descend into them
# and the `!*.dvc` rule cannot reach a pointer file written inside. Re-include the directory,
# re-exclude its contents, and let the final `!*.dvc` rule take the pointer files. The measurement
# files themselves stay ignored exactly as before; the six that were negated above are tracked
# already, and .gitignore does not apply to a tracked file.
!data/corpus-20k/gate2/pages/
data/corpus-20k/gate2/pages/*
!data/corpus-20k/gate2/pages-v2/
data/corpus-20k/gate2/pages-v2/*
!*.dvc

# Open corpus release candidate, Phase 6.5 (scripts/revamp/build_release.py). The built dataset and
# its tarball are large, regenerable from data/revamp, and destined for Zenodo or Hugging Face, so
# they stay on the workstation. The four files that describe the release are tracked: the README
# with the schema and per-field provenance, the citation metadata, the licence record and the
# checksums. The `!data/release/**/` line re-includes the directories themselves so git descends
# into them to find those four.
data/release/**
!data/release/**/
!data/release/**/README.md
!data/release/**/CITATION.cff
!data/release/**/LICENSES.md
!data/release/**/SHA256SUMS
data/revamp/promotion/*.out
